# Project Rules — WebRTC Room

## Language & Edition
- Rust edition 2024 (requires Rust 1.85+)
- No `unsafe` unless justified with a `// SAFETY:` comment
- Prefer `thiserror` for error enums, `anyhow` only in `main`/binaries

## Frontend
- Leptos 0.8+ (CSR mode — WebRTC is inherently client-side)
- Semantic HTML only (`<main>`, `<section>`, `<header>`, `<figure>`, `<video>`, `<details>`, etc.)
- CSS: PicoCSS 2.x (no custom framework, utility classes allowed for layout only)
- Styling: minimal custom CSS in a single file, no CSS-in-JS, no Tailwind
- Icons: none for MVP (future: inline SVG spritesheet)
- All user-facing strings: inline for now (future: `rust-i18n` or similar)

## Signaling
- **SSE (Server-Sent Events)** for server → client push — NOT WebSocket
- Regular `POST /signal` for client → server (SDP offers/answers, ICE candidates)
- SSE event types: `peer-joined`, `peer-left`, `offer`, `answer`, `ice-candidate`, `chat-message`
- All signaling payloads are JSON (serde)

## Chat
- Chat messages sent via `POST /api/room/:id/chat?session_id=...`
- Chat history fetched via `GET /api/room/:id/chat/history`
- Chat broadcast to room members via SSE (`chat-message` event)
- Storage behind a `ChatStore` trait — currently `InMemoryChat` (per-room ring buffer, 200 msgs max)
- Future: swap to SQLite/Postgres by implementing `ChatStore` trait
- Messages are persisted immediately (not fire-and-forget) — append to store BEFORE broadcasting

## User Identity (optional)
- No accounts required for MVP
- Optional display name: entered by user, stored in browser cookie `wr_name` (1yr, SameSite=Lax)
- Stable user ID: auto-generated UUID v4, stored in cookie `wr_uid` (1yr, SameSite=Lax)
- Both sent in `JoinRequest.display_name` and `JoinRequest.user_id`
- Server stores display names per-room (in-memory DashMap)
- Cookie-based identity gives: consistent name across visits, trackable ID for moderation
- Future: cookie ID becomes the `sub` claim in a JWT when auth is added

## WebRTC
- `RTCPeerConnection` via `web-sys` (no JS glue files unless absolutely necessary)
- STUN: always configured (coturn or Google public for dev)
- TURN: ephemeral HMAC credentials served from `GET /api/turn-credentials`
- Media: audio + video (camera) by default, screen share as toggle
- Codec: prefer VP8, fallback to H264 (browser handles negotiation)
- Data channels: enabled for future collaborative features (drawing, reactions)
- No server-side media processing (no SFU for MVP — mesh up to ~4 peers)

## Server
- Framework: Axum 0.8 (paired with Leptos 0.8 fullstack)
- Async runtime: tokio
- State: `Arc<DashMap<String, Room>>` — in-memory, no DB
- SSE: `axum::response::Sse` + `tokio_stream::wrappers::UnboundedReceiverStream`
- CORS: same-origin only (no cross-origin for MVP)
- Graceful shutdown: `tokio::signal::ctrl_c` + `axum::serve` with graceful handle

## Build & Deploy
- Build: `trunk build` for client bundle, `cargo build --release` for server binary
- Single binary deploys: server binary + static files in `dist/`
- coturn: separate process (not embedded)
- Reverse proxy: Caddy or Nginx for TLS (required — WebRTC mandates secure context)
- Docker: single-stage Dockerfile for server, coturn via `network_mode: host`

## File Naming
- Snake_case for modules (`room.rs`, `webrtc.rs`)
- PascalCase for components/types (`RoomPage`, `PeerState`)
- CSS classes: kebab-case only (`video-tile`, `room-controls`)

## Testing
- `#[cfg(test)]` for unit tests
- Integration tests hit real Axum server via `axum::test` helpers
- WebRTC logic: testable as pure Rust where possible (state machines, signaling message routing)

## Security
- TURN credentials: ephemeral (HMAC-SHA1 with TTL per TURN REST API spec — this is a protocol constraint, not a weakness; HMAC security is independent of hash collision resistance)
- Internal hashing (user IDs, future tokens): SHA-256 (sha2 crate)
- Password comparison: `constant_time_eq` crate (not `==`)
- SSE connection: authenticated on connect, re-validated on each signal POST
- No secrets in client bundle (TURN secret stays server-side)
- Input validation: room name regex `[a-z0-9-]{3,48}`, password max 128 chars, display name max 64 chars, chat message max 2000 chars
- Cookies: `SameSite=Lax`, `Path=/`, 1-year expiry — no `Secure` in dev (add via reverse proxy)
